  "term": "pure consciousness",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, pure consciousness means the bare awareness of “I” that is implied in every act of knowing. It is presented as an empty form of self-consciousness that unifies experience but, by itself, does not tell us any positive facts about the self or soul.",
